<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">11 December in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 11 December, from 220 to 1941.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/han-dynasty.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">220 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,806 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Emperor Xian abdicates, ending the Han dynasty</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Emperor Xian, the last emperor of the Eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han dynasty</a> and long a puppet of warlords, was forced to abdicate by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cao-pi">Cao Pi</a>, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cao-cao">Cao Cao</a>. Cao Pi founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cao-wei">Wei dynasty</a>, opening the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/three-kingdoms-period">Three Kingdoms period</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-xian-of-han">Emperor Xian of Han</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cao-pi">Cao Pi</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">361 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,665 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Julian enters Constantinople as sole Roman emperor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Julian entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> as sole emperor and, despite his rejection of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a>, presided over the Christian burial of Constantius, escorting the body to the Church of the Apostles. The act demonstrated his lawful right to the throne.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julian-emperor">Julian</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/861">861 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,165 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Abbasid caliph al-Mutawakkil is assassinated</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Al-Mutawakkil, the tenth Abbasid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a>, was murdered by Turkish military officers. His death began the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anarchy-at-samarra">Anarchy at Samarra</a>, which lasted until 870 and saw four caliphs made and unmade by rival military groups.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anarchy-at-samarra">Anarchy at Samarra</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/969">969 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,057 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Emperor Nikephoros II Phokas is murdered by John Tzimiskes</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Byzantine emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nikephoros-ii-phokas">Nikephoros II Phokas</a>, who had retaken <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crete">Crete</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a> and conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cilicia">Cilicia</a>, was murdered by his nephew, the general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-i-tzimiskes">John Tzimiskes</a>, who seized the throne as John I.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nikephoros-ii-phokas">Nikephoros II Phokas</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-i-tzimiskes">John I Tzimiskes</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1282">1282 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">744 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Llywelyn ap Gruffudd, last native Prince of Wales, is killed</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/llywelyn-ap-gruffudd">Llywelyn ap Gruffudd</a> was killed near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cilmeri">Cilmeri</a> during Edward I's conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a>. Wales lost its independence, and in 1301 Edward gave the title <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-of-wales">Prince of Wales</a> to his own son.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1688">1688 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">338 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">James II flees London</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">As William of Orange advanced, James II slipped out of Whitehall and dropped the Great Seal into the Thames. Caught at Faversham, he escaped to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> later that month; Parliament treated his flight as abdication.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1792">1792 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">234 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Louis XVI goes on trial before the National Convention</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The deposed king, now called Louis Capet, appeared before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-convention">National Convention</a> to answer charges of treason. He was convicted and guillotined in January 1793.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1936">1936 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">90 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Edward VIII abdicates to marry Wallis Simpson</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The abdication took legal effect, and that evening Edward broadcast that he could not reign 'without the help and support of the woman I love'. His brother succeeded as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-vi">George VI</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1941">1941 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">85 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Germany and Italy declare war on the United States</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Four days after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attack-on-pearl-harbor">Pearl Harbor</a>, Hitler and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benito-mussolini">Mussolini</a> declared war on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>. The decision brought American power fully into the war in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 11 December <span class="n">2</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/eberhard-i-duke-of-wurttemberg"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/eberhard-i-duke-of-wurttemberg.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Eberhard I, Duke of Württemberg</span><span class="tp">1445–1496</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/aleksandr-solzhenitsyn"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/aleksandr-solzhenitsyn.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Aleksandr Solzhenitsyn</span><span class="tp">1918–2008</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 11 December <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/llywelyn-ap-gruffudd"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/llywelyn-ap-gruffudd.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Llywelyn ap Gruffudd</span><span class="tp">c. 1223–1282</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-iv-of-castile"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-iv-of-castile.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Henry IV of Castile</span><span class="tp">1425–1474</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/louis-grand-conde"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/louis-grand-conde.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Louis, Grand Condé</span><span class="tp">1621–1686</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jaan-anvelt"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jaan-anvelt.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Jaan Anvelt</span><span class="tp">1884–1937</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ravi-shankar"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ravi-shankar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ravi Shankar</span><span class="tp">1920–2012</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
